WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.737
Missing data can appear in several forms.

00:00:02.737 --> 00:00:05.007
NULL is a database null.

00:00:05.007 --> 00:00:07.682
Blank text is still a string value.

00:00:07.682 --> 00:00:14.187
A sentinel such as all zeros is an ordinary value unless the business rule says it represents missingness.

00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:19.167
The word Unknown is also ordinary text unless its meaning is documented.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:24.587
Do not collapse these states automatically without understanding the source convention.

00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:29.472
Missingness has several representations: NULL, blank text, whitespace,

00:00:29.472 --> 00:00:31.712
and sometimes sentinel codes such as Unknown or 999.

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:34.592
Do not collapse them blindly.

00:00:34.592 --> 00:00:40.092
First decide whether they mean the same thing in the source system,

00:00:40.092 --> 00:00:44.400
then normalize deliberately and keep lineage when the original value may matter.
